WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.746
Hi! If it rains tomorrow, what will you do? And if you had wings? Today we'll learn three common kinds of if sentences.

2
00:00:10.896 --> 00:00:19.338
The first kind talks about facts, things that are always true. If you heat ice, it melts. Both parts use the present tense.

3
00:00:19.488 --> 00:00:30.738
The second kind talks about something that could really happen in the future. If it rains, we will stay home. The if part uses the present tense, and the other part uses will plus a verb.

4
00:00:30.888 --> 00:00:43.026
The third kind is for imaginary or unlikely things. If I had wings, I would fly. The if part uses the past tense, and the other part uses would plus a verb.

5
00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:49.578
In Primary 5, the second kind comes up most. If you study hard, you will pass.

6
00:00:49.728 --> 00:00:55.146
If she is free, she will help us. In the if part we use is, not will be.

7
00:00:55.296 --> 00:01:04.434
The if part can come second too: We will go to the zoo if the weather is fine. When the if part comes first, add a comma after it.

8
00:01:04.584 --> 00:01:12.066
Unless means if not. Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus. That means if you don't hurry, you'll miss it.

9
00:01:12.216 --> 00:01:16.266
It's the same as: If you don't hurry, you will miss the bus.

10
00:01:16.416 --> 00:01:24.474
For imaginary situations, schools usually teach If I were: If I were a bird, I would fly to you.

11
00:01:24.624 --> 00:01:29.058
Watch out! If it will rain, we will stay home is wrong!

12
00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:34.530
Even though the if part is about the future, it uses the present tense: If it rains.

13
00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.594
Will goes only in the other part: we will stay home.

14
00:01:39.744 --> 00:01:50.874
Your turn! If you ___ red and white, you get pink, using the verb mix. What goes in? Pause and think.

15
00:01:51.024 --> 00:01:59.082
The answer is mix. It's a fact, so both parts use the present tense. Did you get it right?

16
00:01:59.232 --> 00:02:10.242
Another one! If we leave now, we ___ the train, using the verb catch. What goes in? Pause and think.

17
00:02:10.392 --> 00:02:15.426
The answer is will catch. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:15.576 --> 00:02:27.018
Try this one! If it ___ sunny tomorrow, we will go swimming, using the verb be. What goes in? Pause and think.

19
00:02:27.168 --> 00:02:36.738
The answer is is. Even though it's about tomorrow, the if part still uses the present tense, not will be. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:36.888 --> 00:02:48.858
Last one! If I ___ a million dollars, I would build a big library, using the verb have. What goes in? Pause and think.

21
00:02:49.008 --> 00:02:56.394
The answer is had, because it's imaginary and the other part uses would. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:56.544 --> 00:03:12.186
Remember: for facts, use the present in both parts. For a real future possibility, use the present in the if part and will in the other. For imaginary things, use the past in the if part and would in the other. Never put will in the if part.

23
00:03:12.336 --> 00:03:17.754
Think about it: If you had a superpower, what would you do?

